<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Satricum</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Satricum was an ancient town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latium">Latium</a>, at Borgo Le Ferriere near Latina south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, contested between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latins</a> and Volsci in the 5th and 4th centuries BCE. Its temple of Mater Matuta yielded the Lapis Satricanus, a Latin inscription of about 500 BCE naming the companions of a Publius Valerius, possibly Publius Valerius Publicola, one of the earliest Latin texts.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/satricum.jpg" alt="Satricum" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: self · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Satricum_1983.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
